---
/**
 * Pre-footer E-E-A-T / medical disclaimer card (YMYL trust signal).
 * Editorial attribution + folklore disclaimer + authoritative clinical
 * references. All outbound links are nofollow (link equity stays internal).
 */
---
<aside
  class="section-shell mt-16"
  aria-labelledby="trust-title"
>
  <div
    class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-plum-700/15 bg-white/70 p-6 shadow-[0_20px_45px_-25px_rgba(69,2,79,.35)] ring-1 ring-white/60 backdrop-blur sm:p-9"
  >
    <div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0">
      <div class="absolute -top-16 -right-10 h-48 w-48 rounded-full bg-girl-200/40 blur-3xl"></div>
      <div class="absolute -bottom-20 -left-14 h-48 w-48 rounded-full bg-boy-100/50 blur-3xl"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="relative">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <span
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-plum-800 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold tracking-wide text-white shadow-[0_8px_18px_-6px_rgba(69,2,79,.5)]"
        >
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 2l2.4 5.1 5.6.7-4.1 3.9 1 5.5-4.9-2.7-4.9 2.7 1-5.5L4 7.8l5.6-.7z"></path>
          </svg>
          Editorial Review
        </span>
        <p id="trust-title" class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-plum-900">
          Researched and compiled by our Parenting &amp; Lunar Astrology Research Team
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-plum-700">
        Every explanation, chart value and date conversion on this site was researched and compiled by our
        Parenting &amp; Lunar Astrology Research Team and fact-checked against published demographic studies,
        including the
        <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20618730/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
          class="font-semibold underline decoration-plum-700 decoration-2 underline-offset-2 hover:text-plum-900"
        >2010 Swedish population registry analysis (2.8 million births)</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-4 rounded-2xl bg-white/80 p-5 ring-1 ring-plum-700/10">
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-plum-700">
          <strong class="font-display text-plum-900">Folklore &amp; medical disclaimer.</strong>
          The Chinese Baby Predictor is an ancient folkloric tool based on traditional Qing Dynasty lunar methods and
          is designed strictly for cultural curiosity and entertainment purposes. It does not provide medical
          diagnosis, fetal sex determination, or reproductive planning. For medically accurate sex determination,
          consult a licensed healthcare provider regarding ultrasound, Non-Invasive Prenatal Testing (NIPT), or
          amniocentesis — see the
          <a href="https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/prenatal-genetic-screening-tests" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
            class="font-semibold underline decoration-girl-400 decoration-2 underline-offset-2 hover:text-plum-900"
          >ACOG prenatal testing guidance</a>
          or
          <a href="https://medlineplus.gov/prenataltesting.html" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
            class="font-semibold underline decoration-girl-400 decoration-2 underline-offset-2 hover:text-plum-900"
          >MedlinePlus: Prenatal Testing</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</aside>
